{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":55,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:03:21.208413Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"edc2b97a-f3b6-4a6e-9bfa-d66c9c21ad48","title":"Fix integrity hydration --repair to actually publish SQLite-only issues to the hub (gh#74)"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":56,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:07:25.623449Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"edc2b97a-f3b6-4a6e-9bfa-d66c9c21ad48","comment_uuid":"e389ec47-f44c-41e1-8168-77e4f2d5c283","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"ROOT CAUSE: check_hydration --repair on v3 (integrity_cmd.rs:335) early-returns with hydrate_from_state only -- re_emit is never called on v3, and re_emit never handled sqlite_only_issues in any case (integrity_drift.rs:362 explicitly skips them, 'populated for reporting only'). So an outage-born sqlite-only issue is preserved LOCALLY by the #427 pass but never published; every hub write for it fails 'not found in v3 state' forever. PLAN: (1) new re_emit_issues() in integrity_drift.rs -- for each sqlite_only_issue load full row+labels+comments+blockers from SQLite, build ImportedIssueSpec (uuid preserved; display_id Some(id) if id>0 else None so the reducer's assign_issue_display_id allocates fresh for negative/collision ids), publish via SharedWriter::import_issues (v3-native single-commit event batch, GH#4 promotion machinery). Returns (old_id,new_id) remap pairs. (2) check_hydration v3 branch: construct SharedWriter BEFORE the v3 early-return; publish issues + run existing re_emit for label/dep/relation/milestone drift; re-read reduced state post-publish; then hydrate_from_state; report published remaps. No writer + drift present + no --accept-data-loss = refuse (mirrors v2 refusal). (3) Extend ImportedIssueSpec with scheduled_at/due_at (IssueCreated event already carries them; import call sites updated) so repair does not silently drop scheduling fields. Comments/time-entries on JSON-known issues remain snapshot-only (unchanged semantics). v2 path unchanged (SharedWriter mutations are refused on v2 by design).","created_at":"2026-08-05T22:07:25.623429Z","kind":"plan"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":57,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:27:44.139238Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"edc2b97a-f3b6-4a6e-9bfa-d66c9c21ad48","comment_uuid":"bf713cfa-b21d-4d04-b658-e56b88653916","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"DECISIONS: (1) Reused migrate to-shared's GH#4 promotion machinery (specs_from_db -> renamed sqlite_only_specs, now pub(crate) + state-driven) rather than writing a parallel publisher in integrity_drift -- one uuid-preserving promotion path, two callers. (2) Display-id policy: positive+free ids carried (reducer adopts, preserving numbering); non-positive ids passed as None so assign_issue_display_id mints a fresh positive id -- repair reports '#-1 -> #N' remaps. (3) DISCOVERED during design: publishing a tombstoned uuid would be silently ignored by the reduction (deletion-wins-forever) and then fail import_issues' post-hydration visibility guard, erroring the whole repair -- added a tombstone filter to sqlite_only_specs, which also fixes the same latent hazard in migrate to-shared. (4) Extended ImportedIssueSpec with scheduled_at/due_at (IssueCreated event already carries them) so repair does not silently drop scheduling fields. (5) v3 repair now: publish issues -> re_emit label/dep/relation/milestone drift -> re-reduce -> hydrate_from_state from the FRESH state (pre-publish state would re-orphan the published rows). No-writer + drift + no --accept-data-loss refuses, mirroring the v2 refusal.","created_at":"2026-08-05T22:27:44.139211Z","kind":"decision"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":58,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:30:16.672659Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"edc2b97a-f3b6-4a6e-9bfa-d66c9c21ad48","comment_uuid":"6d3de622-93cf-45a2-814d-4f3b45036544","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"[action] gh#74 fix implemented on fix/74-hydration-repair-publish-sqlite-only: v3 repair publishes sqlite-only issues via GH#4 promotion; clippy+fmt clean; full suite running","created_at":"2026-08-05T22:30:16.672624Z","kind":"note"}}
