{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":89,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T04:03:54.053824Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"98fe06cc-c504-468b-b59c-47700cf9c077","title":"Daemon bootstrap spawns ~615 git processes on an empty repo; on macOS with /usr/bin/git that takes 16-27 s and fails the 15 s daemon_readiness cap"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":90,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T04:04:25.479248Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"98fe06cc-c504-468b-b59c-47700cf9c077","comment_uuid":"a24599fd-d3a5-4b5e-bd79-f7e9c5a9297d","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Root cause located 2026-09-29. The failures are not sandbox-related (reproduced unsandboxed) and not caused by #65 (identical on a clean 973e395dc worktree). Bootstrapping a fresh one-commit repository with 'daemon ensure --wait-ready' runs 615 git subprocesses: 226 'cat-file -t', 155 'rev-parse --verify', 25 'remote', 22 for-each-ref, 20 'cat-file blob', 14 'ls-remote .', 13 'fetch --no-tags', and others. A stack sample during the stall sits in reconcile::publication::validate_source_objects -> validate_object_type (publication.rs:2554, one 'git cat-file -t' per object, re-run on every pin_source). On this machine /usr/bin/git is Apple's xcrun shim at ~38 ms per spawn: bootstrap takes 27 s through the shim and 16 s calling /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git directly, both over daemon_readiness's 15 s DAEMON_PROCESS_TIMEOUT. CI's macOS runner passes, most likely because of faster git spawns there. The durable fix is batching object validation (one 'git cat-file --batch-check' per pass) and memoizing validated OIDs across pin_source calls; the same per-object spawn pattern explains the ~5-minute first reconciliation on large hubs that motivated ENSURE_WAIT_READY_DEADLINE_SECS.","created_at":"2026-09-29T04:04:25.423209Z","kind":"observation"}}
