{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":99,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T21:45:04.733222Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6f6ad32b-04ec-4164-a36e-ea5b319d73db","comment_uuid":"a52f2659-d671-4cc6-a6ec-f6eac4a2397d","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"[action] Reset done: global crosslink = clean 973e395dc, override removed, daemons restarted on it; kickoff leftovers cleaned (branches + #68 lock remain). Review verdicts: agent_seq seeding = real upstream bug (compact prunes own ref, writer reseeds at 1); GH token = real gap; timeouts = workarounds.","created_at":"2026-10-01T21:45:04.704078Z","kind":"note"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":100,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:31:47.734587Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7c480920-649e-44fa-bf38-2a1788982af6","title":"Daemon exits when its readiness record is more than 90 s old, so any suspend (laptop sleep, SIGSTOP) kills it and blocks all work until a manual ensure","description":"Reproduced 2026-10-01 on build 973e395dc. The daemon refreshes its readiness record every ~35 s (FLUSH_INTERVAL_SECS=30 plus work). readiness.rs MAX_RECORD_AGE_SECONDS=90. In daemon.rs run_normal_loop, each tick calls acquire_housekeeping_operation, which validates the existing record first; if the record is older than 90 s the tick returns 'readiness record is stale' through '?' and the daemon process exits. The daemon is the only refresher, so any stall longer than 90 s is fatal. Repro: SIGSTOP the daemon mid-wait for 100 s, SIGCONT; it exits within 4 s with 'Error: readiness record is stale' in .crosslink/daemon.log. Real-world trigger: macOS sleep. pmset log shows Idle Sleep 15:01:46 to wake 15:04:24 PDT; last record 15:01:37; daemon.log error written 15:04. Also matches the 13:46 wake today and the 18:43 wake on 2026-09-28. After the daemon exits, work-check blocks every Bash/Edit call with 'readiness is unknown' until someone runs 'crosslink daemon ensure --wait-ready --json'. No test or code path handles suspend (grep for suspend finds nothing). Expected: the daemon re-validates and refreshes (or re-reconciles) after a stall instead of exiting; or hooks start the daemon automatically.","priority":"high","created_by":"anon-d38ea320"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":101,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:32:00.136256Z","event":{"type":"LabelAdded","issue_uuid":"7c480920-649e-44fa-bf38-2a1788982af6","label":"bug"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":102,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:32:28.967322Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8414c517-2b10-4966-a48f-61f79e3669f4","comment_uuid":"6d9e5f2a-d844-4522-9f65-87251043b279","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Correction to the 2026-09-29 and 2026-10-01 observations on this issue. The 'readiness unknown / daemon stopped' drops are explained by #69: the daemon exits when its record is over 90 s old, and this Mac idle-sleeps after 1 minute (pmset sleep=1). SessionStart does not fail to repair anything; the daemon was already dead or about to die after a wake. Separate, transient case: 'readiness record projection frontier is stale' with a live daemon appears for up to ~35 s after another checkout sharing this .git (a kickoff worktree) writes hub refs; the daemon's next tick re-hydrates and refreshes (seen 2026-10-01 14:20 PDT: same daemon epoch 7cfdcc6f reported ready again with no restart). The earlier 'mixed builds' theory was wrong (both builds had identical source).","created_at":"2026-10-01T22:32:28.937808Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":103,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:32:45.108113Z","event":{"type":"LockReleased","issue_display_id":65}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":104,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T22:32:59.032688Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"6f6ad32b-04ec-4164-a36e-ea5b319d73db","comment_uuid":"0550edd0-681b-45ae-b7e2-ebff284fb1a0","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Investigated readiness on build 973e395dc. Confirmed #69 (daemon exits after any stall over 90 s; macOS sleep triggers it; reproducible with SIGSTOP). Install verified current: workflow diff and init --update --dry-run show hooks match the build; doctor and integrity pass except stale locks. Open: fork PR #8 (#65) decision, #66 hook rewiring PR, #67 slow git spawns, timeout reverts, upstream report for #69. Two empty kickoff branches still need deleting by the user.","created_at":"2026-10-01T22:32:59.003369Z","kind":"handoff"}}
