{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":110,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T23:01:49.309756Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7c480920-649e-44fa-bf38-2a1788982af6","comment_uuid":"a629e98d-5414-4b6f-bd3f-2fefa6baf2a4","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Second-trigger test, variant A: this write was held for 100 s after publishing its event, then allowed to finish, to see whether the daemon survives a slow successful write.","created_at":"2026-10-01T23:01:49.293402Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":111,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T23:05:37.558022Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7c480920-649e-44fa-bf38-2a1788982af6","comment_uuid":"a6be6805-2bdc-4e42-ad21-0666bbffffe9","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Second-trigger test, variant B: this write was held for 100 s after publishing its event and then killed, to see whether the daemon survives a slow write that never finishes.","created_at":"2026-10-01T23:05:37.541048Z","kind":"observation"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":112,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T23:17:25.828440Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7c480920-649e-44fa-bf38-2a1788982af6","comment_uuid":"3a146b70-5a6a-4a04-a58e-8e3f8f7176a1","author":"anon-d38ea320","content":"Second trigger reproduced 2026-10-01 (build 973e395dc). Method: a PATH shim delayed one 'crosslink issue comment' for 100 s immediately after its agent-ref push; the daemon was not touched. Variant A (write then finishes): the daemon wrote no readiness record for 114 s, 'daemon status' reported 'readiness record projection frontier is stale' and then 'readiness record is stale' for the whole period (all other work in the checkout blocked), and the daemon survived because the finishing write refreshed the record. Variant B (write killed with SIGKILL after the 100 s): the daemon exited 15 s later with 'Error: readiness record is stale'. Mechanism: while a mutation permit is active the daemon's refresh is skipped once the frontier has moved (refresh_ready_record_with returns false when validate_record fails); if the writer never completes its own refresh, the next tick's acquire_housekeeping_operation finds the record over 90 s old and the daemon exits. So #69 has two triggers: daemon suspended over 90 s, and a write that fails or is killed more than about 90 s after publishing. Evidence log: session scratchpad trigger2/result.log.","created_at":"2026-10-01T23:17:25.801396Z","kind":"result"}}
{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":113,"timestamp":"2026-10-01T23:26:03.484024Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1ad8dcf4-51a7-406b-8c3d-65b875a6732b","title":"Return mdatron and vsdd-cli to stock crosslink hook wiring and rule files; drop the fork's 30-minute readiness wait","description":"Operator decision 2026-10-01: no custom crosslink setup. (1) mdatron and vsdd-cli .claude/settings.json: restore the stock hook commands (skip when the hook file is missing) in place of the fail-closed 'payload missing' guard, which blocks every tool call in a plain git worktree. (2) Empty the rule files that only retain the old bundled 0.8 text (stock is zero bytes); vsdd-cli rules/project.md is operator-authored project rules in the designed extension point and stays. (3) Fork: remove ensure_and_wait / the 1800 s bound entirely (fork PR #8 becomes that revert). Prepared from the crosslink session as branches for the operator to push.","priority":"medium","created_by":"anon-d38ea320"}}
