{"agent_id":"anon-d38ea320","agent_seq":154,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:52:00.506668Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"bbad61bf-e465-4fcb-91b2-1e668175f319","title":"Daemon exits with 'refusing to publish ready state for a stale projection' when another checkout publishes during its housekeeping tick","description":"Observed 2026-10-06 19:48 UTC on 875066ad6 while a kickoff container agent (J4Fq, sharing this repository's .git) wrote a comment and then ended its session. Host daemon.log: 'hub reconciliation already current at generation aadb...' then 'Error: refusing to publish ready state for a stale projection'; the daemon exited and every host command was blocked until ensure. Mechanism: the housekeeping tick hydrates, validates, then write_record re-checks projection_is_current; the authority moved between the check and the write, write_record bailed, and run_normal_loop propagated the error out of the daemon. Same class as #69 (#106 upstream): a transient condition during housekeeping is treated as fatal. Fix: a housekeeping failure of this kind should re-run reconciliation (the path #107 added for an expired record) instead of exiting.","priority":"high","created_by":"anon-d38ea320"}}
